# shlink.dadl — Shlink REST API v3 for ToolMesh
# Shlink is a self-hosted URL shortener (https://shlink.io). This file covers
# its REST API v3: short URLs, dynamic redirect rules, tags, visit tracking
# (incl. orphan visits), domains and the health endpoint.
#
# Domain Notes for LLM consumers:
# - SELF-HOSTED: there is no central Shlink service. Every instance has its own
#   address, so base_url is omitted and comes from the backends.yaml url field:
#   the bare instance origin (e.g. https://s.example.com), WITHOUT /rest. The
#   tool paths carry /rest/v3/...; get_health lives at /rest/health
#   (unversioned, works without a key). /rest/v1 and /rest/v2 still answer on
#   Shlink 5.x, but v3 is the current version and the only one used here.
#   Point url at the Shlink SERVER, not at the Shlink web client (the admin
#   UI, often on a separate host): the web client is a single-page app that
#   answers every path, /rest/... included, with its index.html and HTTP 200,
#   so every tool then "succeeds" with an HTML page instead of JSON.
# - AUTH: one API key in the X-Api-Key header. Keys are created on the server
#   with the CLI (shlink api-key:generate); there is no REST endpoint and no UI
#   for key management. Since Shlink 4.3 keys are stored hashed, so the plain
#   key is shown exactly once. Missing header -> 401 missing-authentication;
#   unknown, disabled or expired key -> 401 invalid-api-key.
# - KEY ROLES: a key without roles is an ADMIN key and may do everything.
#   Restricted keys (roles combinable): AUTHORED_SHORT_URLS (--author-only)
#   only sees short URLs it created itself; DOMAIN_SPECIFIC
#   (--domain-only=<domain>) is pinned to one non-default domain;
#   NO_ORPHAN_VISITS (--no-orphan-visits) gets an empty orphan visit list and
#   deletes 0. Non-admin keys get 403 forbidden-tag-operation on rename_tag
#   and delete_tags, and set_domain_redirects fails for them (Shlink 5.1.8
#   answers 500, not 403). A restricted key sees filtered lists, so "not
#   found" can mean "not visible to this key".
# - IDENTIFIER = short code + domain. A short code is unique per domain only.
#   Short URLs on the default domain need no domain parameter. Short URLs on
#   any other domain need domain=<authority> on get, update, delete, visits
#   and redirect rules, otherwise the API answers 404 short-url-not-found. In
#   results "domain": null means the default domain. The keyword DEFAULT
#   stands for the default domain in the list_short_urls domain filter and the
#   list_domain_visits path; set_domain_redirects rejects it (400) and needs
#   the real authority.
# - NORMALIZATION (verified against Shlink 5.1.8): customSlug is slugified
#   (spaces and "/" become "-", case is kept in the default strict mode:
#   "Spring Sale" -> "Spring-Sale"); tags are lowercased and slugified
#   ("Mixed Case Tag" -> "mixed-case-tag"). Generated short codes have 5
#   characters by default; shortCodeLength must be >= 4. A slug that is
#   already taken on that domain is a 400 non-unique-slug. A short code
#   cannot be renamed after creation.
# - GET OR CREATE: create_short_url with findIfExists=true returns an existing
#   short URL for the same long URL (and the same optional fields) instead of
#   creating a duplicate.
# - EDIT IS A TRUE PATCH (verified 5.1.8): omitted fields stay unchanged, null
#   clears validSince/validUntil/maxVisits/title, and tags replaces the whole
#   tag list (tags: [] removes all tags; it never appends).
# - EXPIRY: validSince/validUntil/maxVisits do not hide a short URL from the
#   API; it stays listable and gettable. Visitors get a 404 instead and the hit
#   is tracked as an orphan visit of type invalid_short_url.
#   excludeMaxVisitsReached/excludePastValidUntil filter such links out.
# - DATES: ISO-8601 with offset ("2026-10-01T00:00:00+02:00"); a plain date
#   ("2026-10-01") works too. Shlink converts input dates to its configured
#   timezone. PHP also parses relative words such as "tomorrow"; do not rely
#   on that.
# - VISITS: {referer, date, userAgent, visitLocation, potentialBot,
#   visitedUrl, redirectUrl}; orphan visits add type = base_url (the bare
#   domain), invalid_short_url (a single path segment that is no valid short
#   code: unknown, expired or exhausted, but also scanner probes like
#   /wp-login.php) or regular_404 (any other path, e.g. several segments;
#   verified 5.1.8). visitLocation is null unless the instance
#   has a GeoLite2 license key. potentialBot is a User-Agent heuristic. Lists
#   are newest first. Shlink has no server-side aggregation: the
#   summarize_visits composite pages through visits and counts per day,
#   referrer host, country, city and URL.
# - LARGE INSTANCES (verified 2026-10 against a live instance whose visits
#   table is large and mostly orphan visits, MySQL with a tight memory limit):
#   get_visit_stats reads precomputed counters and is always cheap. Visits of
#   one short URL or one tag are found through an index and stay fast.
#   list_domain_visits (and list_non_orphan_visits WITH a domain filter) join
#   visits to short_urls and order by visit id, which can make MySQL walk the
#   whole visits table: itemsPerPage=5 answered in 40 ms, itemsPerPage=500
#   exhausted the database's memory and MySQL was restarted. Keep those pages
#   small or use the per short URL / per tag tools. Every list page also runs
#   a COUNT over all matching rows, so list_orphan_visits counts every orphan
#   visit on each page; its domain filter is a substring match on visitedUrl
#   and excludeBots/type need row reads, i.e. table scans. On such instances
#   take totals from get_visit_stats and do not page through orphan visits.
# - excludeBots TRAP (verified 5.1.8): ANY value, even "false", excludes bots.
#   Pass "true" to exclude them and OMIT the parameter to include them.
#   excludeMaxVisitsReached and excludePastValidUntil on list_short_urls are
#   real booleans.
# - PAGINATION: page-based (page, itemsPerPage) with the envelope
#   {data, pagination: {currentPage, pagesCount, itemsPerPage,
#   itemsInCurrentPage, totalItems}}. ToolMesh cannot auto-follow it because
#   the items are wrapped in an object, so pagination is exposed: the list
#   tools keep the pagination block in their result and the caller pages.
#   itemsPerPage=-1 returns everything. The visit lists return ALL rows when
#   itemsPerPage is omitted, which on a busy instance means hundreds of
#   thousands, so this file sends itemsPerPage=100 unless told otherwise.
# - QUERY ARRAYS: Shlink only accepts PHP array keys (tags[]=x); a plain
#   tags=x is a 400 on list_short_urls and a 500 on delete_tags. ToolMesh
#   sends one value per query key, so the "tags[]" and "excludeTags[]"
#   parameters take ONE tag each. For several tags call once per tag or
#   filter the result; tagsMode/excludeTagsMode are not exposed for that
#   reason.
# - REDIRECT RULES (Shlink 4.0+): an ordered list of {longUrl, conditions[]}
#   per short URL. All conditions of a rule must match (AND). Rules are tried
#   by priority, which is the order in which they were sent (1 first); without
#   a match the visitor goes to the short URL's own longUrl. set_redirect_rules
#   REPLACES the whole list and an empty list removes all rules. Condition
#   types and their fields are listed in the set_redirect_rules description.
# - TAGS stay in list_tags after their last short URL dropped them
#   (shortUrlsCount 0) until delete_tags removes them. delete_tags answers 204
#   for unknown names as well.
# - DELETING a short URL deletes its visits too. An instance may set
#   DELETE_SHORT_URL_THRESHOLD; short URLs with more visits then answer 422.
# - DOMAINS show up in list_domains once a short URL or a redirect config uses
#   them; set_domain_redirects creates the entry implicitly. The "not found"
#   redirects merge: omitted fields are kept, null clears one.
# - ERRORS are RFC 7807 problem details {type, title, detail, status, ...};
#   type is a URI such as https://shlink.io/api/error/short-url-not-found.
#   Others: invalid-data (with invalidElements[]), non-unique-slug,
#   tag-not-found, tag-conflict, domain-not-found, forbidden-tag-operation,
#   invalid-api-key, mercure-not-configured (501). Branch on type, not detail.
# - Shlink has no rate limiting of its own; a 429 can only come from a proxy.
# - Not exposed: the public redirect endpoint /{shortCode} and the tracking
#   pixel /{shortCode}/track (both create real visits), the deprecated
#   GET /rest/v3/short-urls/shorten (API key in the query string), QR codes
#   (removed in Shlink 5.0), and CLI-only functions (API keys, imports,
#   GeoLite updates, short-url:delete-expired).

spec: "https://dadl.ai/spec/dadl-spec-v0.2.md"
credits:
  - "Dunkel Cloud GmbH -- maintainer"
source_name: "Shlink REST API"
source_url: https://api-spec.shlink.io/
date: "2026-10-23"

# ─── Reusable fragments (underscore keys are ignored by ToolMesh) ────────────
_shared:
  shortcode_param: &p-shortcode
    type: string
    in: path
    required: true
    description: "The short code (the path part of the short URL, e.g. abc12 for https://s.example.com/abc12)."

  domain_param: &p-domain
    type: string
    in: query
    description: "Domain (authority) the short code belongs to. Omit for the default domain; required for short URLs on any other domain, otherwise the API answers 404."

  page_param: &p-page
    type: integer
    in: query
    description: "Page number, starting at 1 (the API default)."

  visits_items_param: &p-visit-items
    type: integer
    in: query
    default: 100
    description: "Visits per page. Defaults to 100 here; -1 returns ALL visits (the API's own default), which can be a huge response."

  start_date_param: &p-start-date
    type: string
    in: query
    description: "ISO-8601 date or date-time from which to include items, e.g. 2026-10-01 or 2026-10-01T00:00:00+02:00."

  end_date_param: &p-end-date
    type: string
    in: query
    description: "ISO-8601 date or date-time until which to include items."

  exclude_bots_param: &p-exclude-bots
    type: string
    in: query
    description: "Pass \"true\" to drop visits flagged as potential bots. ANY value excludes bots (even \"false\"), so omit the parameter to include them."

  visit_domain_filter_param: &p-visit-domain
    type: string
    in: query
    description: "Only count visits on this domain (authority, or DEFAULT for the default domain)."

  pagination: &page-pagination
    strategy: page
    request:
      page_param: page
      limit_param: itemsPerPage
      limit_default: 100
    behavior: expose
    max_pages: 10

backend:
  name: shlink
  type: rest
  version: "1.0"
  # base_url is intentionally omitted: every Shlink instance is self-hosted.
  # Set the backends.yaml url field to the instance origin (without /rest).
  description: >
    Shlink self-hosted URL shortener REST API v3 — create, edit and delete
    short URLs with custom slugs, tags, expiry dates and visit limits, define
    dynamic redirect rules (device, language, query parameter, IP address,
    geolocation, date, browser), read and summarize visit tracking per short
    URL, tag or domain including orphan visits and bot filtering, manage tags
    and per-domain "not found" redirects, and check instance health.

  coverage:
    endpoints: 23
    total_endpoints: 26
    percentage: 88
    focus: >
      Shlink REST API v3: short URLs (custom slugs, tags, expiry, visit
      limits, title, query forwarding), visits (per short URL, tag, domain,
      orphan visits, bot filtering, visit summaries), tags (stats, rename),
      redirect rules (device, language, query param, IP address, geolocation,
      date, browser), domains (not-found redirects), health.
    missing: >
      The public redirect endpoint /{shortCode} and the tracking pixel
      /{shortCode}/track (visitor-facing, both create real visits), the
      deprecated GET /short-urls/shorten (API key in the query string), and
      multi-tag filters with tagsMode/excludeTagsMode (one tag per call).
      API key management, imports and GeoLite updates exist only in the
      Shlink CLI; QR codes were removed from Shlink in 5.0.
    last_reviewed: "2026-10-23"

  setup:
    credential_steps:
      - "Shlink API keys are created with the Shlink CLI on the server, not in a UI. For the official Docker image run: docker exec -it <shlink-container> shlink api-key:generate --name=toolmesh"
      - "Copy the printed key right away. Shlink stores keys hashed and cannot show the key again."
      - "A key without roles is an admin key and works with every tool here. For least privilege add --author-only (only short URLs this key created), --domain-only=s.example.com (one non-default domain) or --no-orphan-visits; such keys cannot rename or delete tags or set domain redirects."
      - "Optional expiry: --expiration-date=2027-12-31. Revoke a key later with shlink api-key:disable <name>."
      - "Fresh container without shell access: start it once with INITIAL_API_KEY=<key-of-your-choice> to seed an admin key."
      - "Put the key into the ToolMesh .env as CREDENTIAL_SHLINK_API_KEY and add the backends.yaml entry with your instance URL."
    env_var: CREDENTIAL_SHLINK_API_KEY
    backends_yaml: |
      - name: shlink
        transport: rest
        dadl: shlink.dadl
        url: "https://s.example.com"
    required_scopes:
      - "Admin API key (no roles) for the full tool set"
    optional_scopes:
      - "AUTHORED_SHORT_URLS role (--author-only): only short URLs created with this key"
      - "DOMAIN_SPECIFIC role (--domain-only=<domain>): only one non-default domain"
      - "NO_ORPHAN_VISITS role (--no-orphan-visits): orphan visits hidden"
    docs_url: "https://shlink.io/documentation/api-docs/authentication/"
    notes: >
      Shlink is self-hosted: set url to the origin that serves /rest of your
      instance (usually the short domain, e.g. https://s.example.com) without
      a /rest suffix. Do not use the address of the Shlink web client (admin
      UI): it answers every request with its HTML start page and HTTP 200, so
      the tools return HTML instead of JSON. Check with
      https://<your-host>/rest/health, which must return JSON with status
      pass. Requires Shlink 3.0 or newer for REST API v3; redirect
      rules need 4.0, the date conditions 5.0 and the browser condition 5.1.
      Verified against Shlink 5.1.8. Geolocation fields and the geolocation
      redirect conditions need a GeoLite2 license key on the Shlink server.
      The health endpoint needs no key.

  auth:
    type: apikey
    credential: shlink_api_key
    inject_into: header
    header_name: X-Api-Key

  defaults:
    headers:
      # Shlink may answer an unexpected error with HTML unless JSON is asked for.
      Accept: application/json
    content_type: application/json
    pagination: *page-pagination
    errors:
      format: json
      message_path: "$.detail"
      code_path: "$.type"
      # Shlink itself does not rate-limit; 429/502/504 come from a proxy in
      # front of it. 503 is also what get_health returns while the database is
      # unreachable.
      retry_on: [429, 502, 503, 504]
      terminal: [400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 422, 501]
      retry_strategy:
        max_retries: 3
        backoff: exponential
        initial_delay: 1s
    response:
      result_path: "$"

  tools:
    # ── Short URLs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_short_urls:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls
      access: read
      description: >
        List short URLs, newest first by default. Returns {data: ShortUrl[],
        pagination: {currentPage, pagesCount, itemsPerPage, itemsInCurrentPage,
        totalItems}}; page through with page. Each ShortUrl has shortCode,
        shortUrl, longUrl, dateCreated, tags, meta {validSince, validUntil,
        maxVisits}, domain (null = default domain), title, crawlable,
        forwardQuery, hasRedirectRules and visitsSummary {total, nonBots,
        bots}. Expired or exhausted links are included unless the exclude*
        flags are set. Tag filters take ONE tag each (Shlink needs the PHP
        array key "tags[]"; call again for another tag).
      params:
        page: *p-page
        itemsPerPage:
          type: integer
          in: query
          default: 50
          description: "Short URLs per page. Defaults to 50 here (API default 10); -1 returns all."
        searchTerm:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Substring searched in longUrl, shortCode and title."
        "tags[]":
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Only short URLs carrying this ONE tag (a single string, not an array). Tags are lowercase slugs."
        "excludeTags[]":
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Only short URLs WITHOUT this ONE tag (a single string, not an array)."
        orderBy:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Sort order: longUrl-ASC|DESC, shortCode-ASC|DESC, dateCreated-ASC|DESC, title-ASC|DESC, visits-ASC|DESC, nonBotVisits-ASC|DESC (e.g. visits-DESC for the most clicked links)."
        startDate:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Only short URLs created on or after this ISO-8601 date or date-time."
        endDate:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Only short URLs created on or before this ISO-8601 date or date-time."
        excludeMaxVisitsReached:
          type: boolean
          in: query
          description: "true hides short URLs that already reached maxVisits."
        excludePastValidUntil:
          type: boolean
          in: query
          description: "true hides short URLs whose validUntil lies in the past."
        domain:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Only short URLs of this domain (authority), or DEFAULT for the default domain."
        apiKeyName:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Only short URLs created with the API key of this name. Admin keys only; ignored for other keys unless it is their own name."
      response:
        result_path: "$.shortUrls"

    create_short_url:
      method: POST
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls
      access: write
      description: >
        Create a short URL and return the ShortUrl object (its shortUrl field is
        the link to hand out). Without customSlug Shlink generates a 5-character
        code (shortCodeLength >= 4). customSlug is slugified: spaces and "/"
        become "-". Tags are lowercased and slugified. A slug already used on
        that domain fails with 400 non-unique-slug; invalid input fails with
        400 invalid-data listing invalidElements. Set findIfExists=true to get
        an existing short URL for the same long URL (and same optional fields)
        back instead of creating a duplicate.
      params:
        longUrl:
          type: string
          in: body
          required: true
          description: "The URL to redirect to (absolute http/https URL)."
        customSlug:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "Own short code instead of a generated one, e.g. spring-sale."
        pathPrefix:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "Prefix prepended to the custom slug or generated code, e.g. promo."
        findIfExists:
          type: boolean
          in: body
          description: "true returns a matching existing short URL instead of creating a new one."
        domain:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "Domain (authority) the short URL belongs to; omit for the default domain. Ignored for domain-restricted keys."
        shortCodeLength:
          type: integer
          in: body
          description: "Length of the generated code, at least 4 (default 5). Ignored when customSlug is set."
        validSince:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "ISO-8601 date-time from which the short URL redirects; earlier visits get a 404."
        validUntil:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "ISO-8601 date-time after which the short URL stops redirecting."
        maxVisits:
          type: integer
          in: body
          description: "Number of visits after which the short URL stops redirecting."
        tags:
          type: array
          in: body
          description: "Tag names, e.g. [\"campaign\", \"newsletter\"]. Missing tags are created."
        title:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "Descriptive title. If omitted, the server may fetch the page title when title auto-resolution is enabled there."
        crawlable:
          type: boolean
          in: body
          description: "true lists the short URL as Allow in Shlink's robots.txt (default false)."
        forwardQuery:
          type: boolean
          in: body
          description: "Forward query parameters of the short URL to the long URL (default true)."
      pagination: none

    get_short_url:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls/{shortCode}
      access: read
      description: >
        Get one short URL by short code: longUrl, tags, meta {validSince,
        validUntil, maxVisits}, title, crawlable, forwardQuery,
        hasRedirectRules and visitsSummary {total, nonBots, bots}. Short URLs on
        a non-default domain need the domain parameter, otherwise 404
        short-url-not-found.
      params:
        shortCode: *p-shortcode
        domain: *p-domain
      pagination: none

    update_short_url:
      method: PATCH
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls/{shortCode}
      access: write
      description: >
        Edit a short URL. True partial update: only the fields sent change,
        omitted fields stay as they are. null clears validSince, validUntil,
        maxVisits or title. tags REPLACES the whole tag list (send the full
        list; [] removes all tags). The short code and domain cannot be changed.
        Returns the updated ShortUrl. Short URLs on a non-default domain need the
        domain parameter.
      params:
        shortCode: *p-shortcode
        domain: *p-domain
        longUrl:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "New target URL."
        validSince:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "ISO-8601 date-time from which the short URL redirects; null clears it."
        validUntil:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "ISO-8601 date-time after which the short URL stops redirecting; null clears it."
        maxVisits:
          type: integer
          in: body
          description: "Visit limit; null removes it."
        tags:
          type: array
          in: body
          description: "Complete new tag list (replaces the existing tags)."
        title:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "New title; null clears it."
        crawlable:
          type: boolean
          in: body
          description: "true lists the short URL as Allow in robots.txt."
        forwardQuery:
          type: boolean
          in: body
          description: "Forward query parameters of the short URL to the long URL."
      pagination: none

    delete_short_url:
      method: DELETE
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls/{shortCode}
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Delete a short URL together with all of its visits. Irreversible; later
        hits on the code become orphan visits. Returns nothing (204). Fails with
        422 when the server has DELETE_SHORT_URL_THRESHOLD set and the short URL
        has more visits than that. Short URLs on a non-default domain need the
        domain parameter.
      params:
        shortCode: *p-shortcode
        domain: *p-domain
      pagination: none

    # ── Redirect rules ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_redirect_rules:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls/{shortCode}/redirect-rules
      access: read
      description: >
        List the dynamic redirect rules of one short URL. Returns
        {defaultLongUrl, redirectRules: [{longUrl, priority, conditions:
        [{type, matchKey, matchValue}]}]}; priority 1 is checked first and
        defaultLongUrl is used when no rule matches. Read this before
        set_redirect_rules when rules should be added rather than replaced.
      params:
        shortCode: *p-shortcode
        domain: *p-domain
      pagination: none

    set_redirect_rules:
      method: POST
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls/{shortCode}/redirect-rules
      access: write
      description: >
        Replace ALL redirect rules of a short URL (an empty array removes every
        rule). Priorities follow the array order. Each rule is {longUrl,
        conditions: [{type, matchKey, matchValue}]}; all conditions of a rule
        must match. Condition types: device (matchValue android, ios, mobile,
        windows, macos, linux, chromeos or desktop); language (matchValue such
        as en or en-US, from Accept-Language); query-param (matchKey = param
        name, matchValue = exact value); any-value-query-param (matchKey =
        param name, present with or without value); valueless-query-param
        (matchKey = param name, present without value); ip-address (matchValue
        exact IP, CIDR like 192.0.2.0/24 or wildcard like 192.0.2.*);
        geolocation-country-code (matchValue ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, e.g. DE);
        geolocation-city-name (matchValue city name); before-date and
        after-date (matchValue ISO-8601 date-time, Shlink 5.0+); browser
        (matchValue chrome, firefox, edge, safari, opera or android_browser,
        Shlink 5.1+). matchKey may be omitted or null where unused. Geolocation
        conditions need GeoLite2 on the server. Returns the resulting rule list
        like list_redirect_rules; an unknown value fails with 400 invalid-data
        whose invalidElements holds the index of the bad rule.
      params:
        shortCode: *p-shortcode
        domain: *p-domain
        redirectRules:
          type: array
          in: body
          required: true
          description: "Ordered rules, e.g. [{\"longUrl\": \"https://example.com/app\", \"conditions\": [{\"type\": \"device\", \"matchValue\": \"mobile\", \"matchKey\": null}]}]."
      pagination: none

    # ── Tags ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_tags:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/tags
      access: read
      description: >
        List tag names, alphabetically by default. Returns {data: string[],
        pagination}. Without itemsPerPage all tags come back in one page.
        Tags stay listed after their last short URL dropped them until
        delete_tags removes them; use list_tag_stats for usage counts.
      params:
        page: *p-page
        itemsPerPage:
          type: integer
          in: query
          description: "Tags per page; omit to get all tags."
        searchTerm:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Substring searched in the tag name."
        orderBy:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "tag-ASC or tag-DESC."
      response:
        result_path: "$.tags"

    list_tag_stats:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/tags/stats
      access: read
      description: >
        List tags with usage statistics. Returns {data: [{tag, shortUrlsCount,
        visitsSummary: {total, nonBots, bots}}], pagination}. Ordering by
        shortUrlsCount or visits is as slow as loading the whole list, so omit
        itemsPerPage when sorting by those.
      params:
        page: *p-page
        itemsPerPage:
          type: integer
          in: query
          description: "Tags per page; omit to get all tags."
        searchTerm:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Substring searched in the tag name."
        orderBy:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "tag-ASC|DESC, shortUrlsCount-ASC|DESC, visits-ASC|DESC or nonBotVisits-ASC|DESC."
      response:
        result_path: "$.tags"

    rename_tag:
      method: PUT
      path: /rest/v3/tags
      access: admin
      description: >
        Rename a tag on every short URL that carries it. Returns nothing (204).
        404 tag-not-found when oldName does not exist, 409 tag-conflict when
        newName is taken (tags cannot be merged this way), 403
        forbidden-tag-operation for non-admin API keys.
      params:
        oldName:
          type: string
          in: body
          required: true
          description: "Current tag name."
        newName:
          type: string
          in: body
          required: true
          description: "New tag name (stored as a lowercase slug)."
      pagination: none

    delete_tags:
      method: DELETE
      path: /rest/v3/tags
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Delete ONE tag (removes it from every short URL; the short URLs stay).
        Returns nothing (204), also for unknown names. Call once per tag.
        Non-admin API keys get 403 forbidden-tag-operation.
      params:
        "tags[]":
          type: string
          in: query
          required: true
          description: "Name of the tag to delete (a single string, not an array)."
      pagination: none

    # ── Visits ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    get_visit_stats:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/visits
      access: read
      description: >
        Instance-wide visit counters: {nonOrphanVisits: {total, nonBots, bots},
        orphanVisits: {total, nonBots, bots}}. Non-orphan visits hit an existing
        short URL; orphan visits hit the bare domain, an unknown or expired
        short code, or any other path. Cheap; use it before pulling visit lists.
      pagination: none
      response:
        result_path: "$.visits"

    list_short_url_visits:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls/{shortCode}/visits
      access: read
      description: >
        List the visits of one short URL, newest first. Returns {data: Visit[],
        pagination}; a Visit is {referer, date, userAgent, visitLocation
        {countryCode, countryName, regionName, cityName, latitude, longitude,
        timezone} or null, potentialBot, visitedUrl, redirectUrl}. 100 per page
        unless itemsPerPage says otherwise. For counts per day, referrer or
        country use the summarize_visits composite instead of paging raw visits.
      params:
        shortCode: *p-shortcode
        domain: *p-domain
        startDate: *p-start-date
        endDate: *p-end-date
        excludeBots: *p-exclude-bots
        page: *p-page
        itemsPerPage: *p-visit-items
      response:
        result_path: "$.visits"

    list_tag_visits:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/tags/{tag}/visits
      access: read
      description: >
        List the visits of all short URLs carrying a tag, newest first. Returns
        {data: Visit[], pagination}, 100 per page by default. 404 tag-not-found
        for an unknown tag.
      params:
        tag:
          type: string
          in: path
          required: true
          description: "Tag name (lowercase slug)."
        domain: *p-visit-domain
        startDate: *p-start-date
        endDate: *p-end-date
        excludeBots: *p-exclude-bots
        page: *p-page
        itemsPerPage: *p-visit-items
      response:
        result_path: "$.visits"

    list_domain_visits:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/domains/{domain}/visits
      access: read
      description: >
        List the visits of all short URLs on one domain, newest first. Returns
        {data: Visit[], pagination}, 20 per page by default. Use DEFAULT as
        domain for the default domain. 404 domain-not-found for an unknown
        domain. EXPENSIVE on instances with a large visits table: MySQL may walk
        the whole table to fill a page, and a 500-item page has exhausted a
        memory-limited database. Keep itemsPerPage small (<= 20) and prefer
        list_short_url_visits or list_tag_visits for analysis.
      params:
        domain:
          type: string
          in: path
          required: true
          description: "Domain authority (e.g. s.example.com) or DEFAULT."
        startDate: *p-start-date
        endDate: *p-end-date
        excludeBots: *p-exclude-bots
        page: *p-page
        itemsPerPage:
          type: integer
          in: query
          default: 20
          description: "Visits per page. Defaults to 20 here; large pages and -1 can overload the database on big instances."
      response:
        result_path: "$.visits"

    list_non_orphan_visits:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/visits/non-orphan
      access: read
      description: >
        List visits to any existing short URL across the instance, newest
        first. Returns {data: Visit[], pagination}, 100 per page by default.
        Fast without the domain filter (index on the short URL reference). The
        domain filter adds the same join as list_domain_visits and can make
        MySQL walk the whole visits table; use small pages with it.
      params:
        domain: *p-visit-domain
        startDate: *p-start-date
        endDate: *p-end-date
        excludeBots: *p-exclude-bots
        page: *p-page
        itemsPerPage: *p-visit-items
      response:
        result_path: "$.visits"

    list_orphan_visits:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/visits/orphan
      access: read
      description: >
        List orphan visits (requests that matched no valid short URL), newest
        first. Returns {data: OrphanVisit[], pagination}, 100 per page by
        default; each item is a Visit plus type: base_url (the bare domain),
        invalid_short_url (a single path segment that is no valid short code,
        i.e. unknown, expired or exhausted codes and scanner probes such as
        /wp-login.php) or regular_404 (any other path, e.g. several segments).
        Scanners and bots usually dominate here. API keys with the
        NO_ORPHAN_VISITS role always get an empty list. Every page runs a COUNT
        over all matching orphan visits; the domain filter (a substring match on
        visitedUrl), excludeBots and type turn that into a table scan. On
        instances with many orphan visits take totals from get_visit_stats.
      params:
        type:
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Only this orphan type: base_url, invalid_short_url or regular_404."
        domain: *p-visit-domain
        startDate: *p-start-date
        endDate: *p-end-date
        excludeBots: *p-exclude-bots
        page: *p-page
        itemsPerPage: *p-visit-items
      response:
        result_path: "$.visits"

    delete_short_url_visits:
      method: DELETE
      path: /rest/v3/short-urls/{shortCode}/visits
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Delete ALL visits of one short URL (the short URL itself stays and its
        counters restart at 0). Irreversible. Returns {deletedVisits: number}.
      params:
        shortCode: *p-shortcode
        domain: *p-domain
      pagination: none

    delete_orphan_visits:
      method: DELETE
      path: /rest/v3/visits/orphan
      access: dangerous
      description: >
        Delete ALL orphan visits of the instance (bot and scanner noise on
        unknown paths). Irreversible; there is no date or type filter. Returns
        {deletedVisits: number}; keys with the NO_ORPHAN_VISITS role get 0.
      pagination: none

    # ── Domains ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_domains:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/domains
      access: read
      description: >
        List the domains in use: {data: [{domain, isDefault, redirects:
        {baseUrlRedirect, regular404Redirect, invalidShortUrlRedirect}}],
        defaultRedirects}. defaultRedirects apply to every domain without its
        own setting; null means Shlink shows its 404 page. A domain appears once
        a short URL or a redirect setting uses it.
      pagination: none
      response:
        result_path: "$.domains"

    set_domain_redirects:
      method: PATCH
      path: /rest/v3/domains/redirects
      access: admin
      description: >
        Set where visitors of a domain go when nothing matches: the bare domain
        (baseUrlRedirect), a single path segment that is no valid short code,
        e.g. an unknown or expired one (invalidShortUrlRedirect), or any other
        path (regular404Redirect).
        Merges with the current values: omitted fields stay, null clears one.
        Creates the domain entry if needed. Needs the real authority (DEFAULT
        is rejected) and an admin API key. Returns the resulting redirects.
      params:
        domain:
          type: string
          in: body
          required: true
          description: "Domain authority, e.g. s.example.com (the default domain too, by its name)."
        baseUrlRedirect:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "URL for visits to the bare domain; null clears it."
        regular404Redirect:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "URL for visits to any other unmatched path (e.g. several segments); null clears it."
        invalidShortUrlRedirect:
          type: string
          in: body
          description: "URL for visits to a single path segment that is no valid short code (unknown, expired or exhausted); null clears it."
      pagination: none

    # ── Integrations and monitoring ──────────────────────────────────────

    get_mercure_info:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/v3/mercure-info
      access: admin
      description: >
        Get the Mercure hub URL and a short-lived subscriber JWT for real-time
        updates (new visits, new short URLs): {mercureHubUrl, jwt,
        jwtExpiration}. The JWT is a credential; do not log or share it. 501
        mercure-not-configured when the instance has no Mercure hub.
      pagination: none

    get_health:
      method: GET
      path: /rest/health
      access: read
      description: >
        Health check of the instance including its database connection:
        {status: pass|fail, version, links}. HTTP 503 with status fail when
        Shlink cannot reach its database. Needs no API key; version shows the
        Shlink release. An HTML page instead of JSON (here and from every other
        tool) means the backend url points at the Shlink web client, not at the
        Shlink server.
      pagination: none

  composites:
    summarize_visits:
      description: >
        Aggregate visits instead of paging raw rows: counts per day, top
        referrer hosts, countries, cities, visited and redirect URLs, bots and
        orphan types. scope selects the source: short_url (needs shortCode,
        plus domain for a non-default domain), tag (needs tag, optional domain),
        non_orphan (all short URLs) or orphan. Reads newest first in pages of
        500, at most maxVisits rows (default 5000, max 20000); truncated=true
        means the counts cover only the newest analyzed visits of
        total_matching. There is deliberately no per-domain scope: that query
        can make MySQL walk the whole visits table. On instances with many
        orphan visits every orphan page counts all of them, so keep maxVisits
        low there and take totals from get_visit_stats.
      access: read
      timeout: 90s
      depends_on: [list_short_url_visits, list_tag_visits, list_orphan_visits, list_non_orphan_visits]
      params:
        scope:
          type: string
          required: true
          description: "short_url, tag, non_orphan or orphan."
        shortCode:
          type: string
          description: "Short code (scope short_url)."
        tag:
          type: string
          description: "Tag name (scope tag)."
        domain:
          type: string
          description: "Domain authority of the short URL (scope short_url, needed for a non-default domain) or domain filter (scope tag, DEFAULT allowed). Ignored for the other scopes."
        orphanType:
          type: string
          description: "Scope orphan only: base_url, invalid_short_url or regular_404. Needs a table scan per page on large instances."
        startDate:
          type: string
          description: "ISO-8601 date or date-time from which to count."
        endDate:
          type: string
          description: "ISO-8601 date or date-time until which to count."
        excludeBots:
          type: boolean
          default: false
          description: "true drops visits flagged as potential bots."
        maxVisits:
          type: integer
          default: 5000
          description: "Maximum number of visits to read (1 to 20000)."
        top:
          type: integer
          default: 10
          description: "Entries per top list."
      code: |
        const scope = params.scope;
        const pageSize = 500;
        const limit = Math.min(Math.max(params.maxVisits || 5000, 1), 20000);
        const topN = Math.min(Math.max(params.top || 10, 1), 100);
        const q = {};
        if (params.startDate) q.startDate = params.startDate;
        if (params.endDate) q.endDate = params.endDate;
        if (params.excludeBots) q.excludeBots = "true";
        let call;
        if (scope === "short_url") {
          if (!params.shortCode) throw new Error("scope short_url needs shortCode");
          q.shortCode = params.shortCode;
          if (params.domain) q.domain = params.domain;
          call = (p) => api.list_short_url_visits(p);
        } else if (scope === "tag") {
          if (!params.tag) throw new Error("scope tag needs tag");
          q.tag = params.tag;
          if (params.domain) q.domain = params.domain;
          call = (p) => api.list_tag_visits(p);
        } else if (scope === "orphan") {
          if (params.orphanType) q.type = params.orphanType;
          call = (p) => api.list_orphan_visits(p);
        } else if (scope === "non_orphan") {
          call = (p) => api.list_non_orphan_visits(p);
        } else {
          throw new Error("scope must be short_url, tag, non_orphan or orphan (there is no per-domain scope: that query can scan the whole visits table)");
        }

        const visits = [];
        let total = 0;
        let page = 1;
        while (visits.length < limit) {
          const res = await call(Object.assign({}, q, { page: page, itemsPerPage: pageSize }));
          const data = (res && res.data) || [];
          const pg = (res && res.pagination) || {};
          total = pg.totalItems || 0;
          for (const v of data) {
            if (visits.length >= limit) break;
            visits.push(v);
          }
          if (data.length === 0 || page >= (pg.pagesCount || 1)) break;
          page++;
        }

        const count = (m, k) => {
          const key = (k === null || k === undefined || k === "") ? "(none)" : String(k);
          m[key] = (m[key] || 0) + 1;
        };
        const host = (u) => {
          if (!u) return null;
          const m = /^[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:\/\/([^\/?#]+)/i.exec(u);
          return m ? m[1].toLowerCase() : u;
        };
        const topOf = (m) => Object.keys(m)
          .map((k) => ({ value: k, count: m[k] }))
          .sort((a, b) => b.count - a.count)
          .slice(0, topN);

        const byDay = {}, referrers = {}, countries = {}, cities = {};
        const visited = {}, redirects = {}, types = {};
        let bots = 0, located = 0;
        for (const v of visits) {
          count(byDay, (v.date || "").slice(0, 10));
          count(referrers, host(v.referer));
          count(visited, v.visitedUrl);
          count(redirects, v.redirectUrl);
          if (v.potentialBot) bots++;
          if (v.type) count(types, v.type);
          const loc = v.visitLocation;
          if (loc && loc.countryCode) {
            located++;
            count(countries, loc.countryCode);
            count(cities, (loc.cityName || "(unknown)") + ", " + loc.countryCode);
          } else {
            count(countries, "(unknown)");
          }
        }

        const result = {
          scope: scope,
          total_matching: total,
          analyzed: visits.length,
          truncated: visits.length < total,
          newest: visits.length ? visits[0].date : null,
          oldest: visits.length ? visits[visits.length - 1].date : null,
          potential_bots: bots,
          with_location: located,
          by_day: Object.keys(byDay).sort().map((d) => ({ date: d, visits: byDay[d] })),
          top_referrer_hosts: topOf(referrers),
          top_countries: topOf(countries),
          top_cities: topOf(cities),
          top_visited_urls: topOf(visited),
          top_redirect_urls: topOf(redirects)
        };
        if (scope === "orphan") result.orphan_types = topOf(types);
        return result;

  examples:
    - name: "Campaign link"
      description: "Get or create a tagged short URL that stops working at the end of the year"
      code: |
        const link = await api.create_short_url({
          longUrl: "https://example.com/landing?utm_source=newsletter",
          customSlug: "newsletter-2026",
          tags: ["newsletter", "campaign-2026"],
          title: "Newsletter landing page",
          validUntil: "2026-12-31T23:59:59+00:00",
          findIfExists: true
        });
        return { shortUrl: link.shortUrl, shortCode: link.shortCode };

    - name: "Add a mobile redirect without losing existing rules"
      description: "set_redirect_rules replaces the whole list, so read, append and write back"
      code: |
        const current = await api.list_redirect_rules({ shortCode: "newsletter-2026" });
        const rules = current.redirectRules.map((r) => ({ longUrl: r.longUrl, conditions: r.conditions }));
        rules.push({
          longUrl: "https://example.com/app",
          conditions: [{ type: "device", matchValue: "mobile", matchKey: null }]
        });
        return await api.set_redirect_rules({ shortCode: "newsletter-2026", redirectRules: rules });

    - name: "Click report for one link"
      description: "Daily clicks, top referrers and countries of a short URL in October, without bots"
      code: |
        return await api.summarize_visits({
          scope: "short_url",
          shortCode: "newsletter-2026",
          startDate: "2026-10-01",
          endDate: "2026-10-31T23:59:59+00:00",
          excludeBots: true,
          top: 5
        });

    - name: "Most clicked links of a tag"
      description: "Rank all short URLs carrying one tag by human (non-bot) visits"
      code: |
        const res = await api.list_short_urls({ "tags[]": "campaign-2026", orderBy: "nonBotVisits-DESC", itemsPerPage: 20 });
        return res.data.map((u) => ({ shortUrl: u.shortUrl, longUrl: u.longUrl, visits: u.visitsSummary.nonBots }));

    - name: "Orphan visit triage"
      description: "Compare orphan and regular traffic, then see which unknown paths are hit most"
      code: |
        const stats = await api.get_visit_stats();
        const orphans = await api.summarize_visits({ scope: "orphan", maxVisits: 500, top: 15 });
        return { stats: stats, orphan_types: orphans.orphan_types, top_paths: orphans.top_visited_urls, truncated: orphans.truncated };
